444
00:27:58,460 --> 00:28:05,100
This is all his expenses, right? My investment is more, so my return is also more, right?

445
00:28:05,180 --> 00:28:11,205
And the employees, if they are today, and tomorrow, God forbid, they get fired,

446
00:28:11,285 --> 00:28:15,340
they can go somewhere else and they lose nothing, essentially.

447
00:28:16,140 --> 00:28:20,900
But whoever is in debt, that person loses everything. Same goes for a factory.

448
00:28:20,980 --> 00:28:24,970
I heard an argument on this on YouTube. So…

449
00:28:25,390 --> 00:28:29,730
Because the risk is more involved, so the return is also higher. High risk, high returns.

450
00:28:29,810 --> 00:28:37,190
Like there was a study in some time that female Uber drivers make 7% less than male counterparts.

451
00:28:37,470 --> 00:28:39,668
Now the reason was that men drive fast.

452
00:28:39,748 --> 00:28:45,060
He drives fast, so he drops faster, picks up more rides, and essentially makes more money.

453
00:28:45,210 --> 00:28:46,630
So high risk, high returns.

454
00:28:46,710 --> 00:28:52,500
So now here also a capitalist can say that my risk is also that much. I have 32,000 employees tomorrow.

455
00:28:52,580 --> 00:28:54,940
If it closes tomorrow, they'll find another job somewhere else.

456
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:56,700
What will I get on the street?

457
00:28:56,780 --> 00:29:00,700
So when my return is high, then I have that too.

458
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:03,740
It is my right that I enjoy according to my own.

459
00:29:03,820 --> 00:29:05,460
I mean, where do you draw the line?

460
00:29:05,540 --> 00:29:11,100
But I think things should be set from above and good examples should always be set from the top.

461
00:29:11,180 --> 00:29:12,580
Because people look up to you.

462
00:29:12,660 --> 00:29:19,680
When you know that you have a global name and you have a global outreach and a whole billion eyes are on you.

463
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:23,880
So one must act in a way that it is a good example for people.

464
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:29,640
Not that you go so far in extravagance that people start to feel cringe.

465
00:29:29,720 --> 00:29:34,040
But nevertheless, congratulations to the Humbanis and to them.

466
00:29:34,120 --> 00:29:35,400
This happiness is very blessed.

467
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:39,800
We pray for you and may Allah make you better for everyone.

468
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:41,920
I hope I answered your question.

469
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:44,600
But if there is anything left, please do tell me in the comments. Thank you.

470
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:46,340
Alright, next question says.

471
00:29:46,420 --> 00:29:48,920
Problems at making small talks at work.

472
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:53,220
Thank you, Junaid Bhai. I hope you're doing great. I am a huge fan of your work, especially towards education.

473
00:29:53,300 --> 00:29:59,020
I'm facing a problem in my workplace, which isn't something huge, but leaves me embarrassed and numb at times.

474
00:29:59,100 --> 00:30:03,220
For background, I work in the pricing department of a firm in Saudi Arabia.

475
00:30:03,300 --> 00:30:07,340
I work as a junior analyst and it's been five months since I've joined the workforce.

476
00:30:07,420 --> 00:30:11,420
The problem is difficulty in making small talks before or in between meetings.

477
00:30:11,500 --> 00:30:14,230
Junaid Bhai, whenever my manager asks on Monday about my week.

478
00:30:14,310 --> 00:30:19,230
How my weekend was, I freeze and go absolutely silent after a few mumblings.

479
00:30:19,310 --> 00:30:26,230
I also find it very hard to communicate during lunch hours and the only refuge I find sometimes is discussing cricket.

480
00:30:26,310 --> 00:30:29,634
I seek your advice on this matter as I do want to perform well,

481
00:30:29,714 --> 00:30:33,567
but as you know work is only the tip of the iceberg in corporate life.

482
00:30:33,647 --> 00:30:34,464
Please advise me.

483
00:30:34,544 --> 00:30:35,310
Warm regards.

484
00:30:41,920 --> 00:30:53,560
If you don't have hobbies, you can't talk.

485
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:55,360
I'll give you a good example.

486
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:58,994
For example, whenever you have a big event,

487
00:30:59,074 --> 00:31:03,840
whether it's a national event or an event in your family,

488
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:09,080
where you have guests at your house or you are sitting at a wedding table, you just talk to your uncles.

489
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:11,466
and see what they talk about.

490
00:31:11,546 --> 00:31:13,931
They will talk about politics.

491
00:31:14,011 --> 00:31:21,645
And then you analyze each and every one of those uncles that what they do in their free time.

492
00:31:21,725 --> 00:31:22,918
They do nothing.

493
00:31:22,998 --> 00:31:25,542
They go to work, they come home,

494
00:31:25,622 --> 00:31:33,490
they put on TV or watch forwards as received on WhatsApp and comment and go to sleep.

495
00:31:33,570 --> 00:31:34,920
So they have no life.

496
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:41,720
There will be no sport, no gym, no activity, no hobby.

497
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:44,680
And because they know that the other person is not doing anything,

498
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:49,600
then they will talk about business and say that business is not good,

499
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:51,640
this is not good, that is not good, they are ruined.

500
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:55,880
And then they will go around saying that same Imran Khan, that same Nawaz Sharif, and there will be no third thing.

501
00:31:55,960 --> 00:31:58,080
And I am saying this across the board.

502
00:31:58,160 --> 00:32:00,640
You can also look at overseas uncles.

503
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:03,120
I always say that they have no hobby.

504
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:07,674
You live in such a good environment that you get two days off,

505
00:32:07,754 --> 00:32:14,920
you have so many activities to do, you just have to get out of the car and go anywhere.

506
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:16,502
There's so much to do.

507
00:32:16,582 --> 00:32:18,151
But people don't do it,

508
00:32:18,231 --> 00:32:23,920
they stay at home and they do TikTok and YouTube and the same videos of politics.

509
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:29,000
Again, when you don't do anything, then you won't have anything to talk about.

510
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:35,340
Now, how many of us are there, I'm talking about Desi people, who like doing gardening?

511
00:32:35,420 --> 00:32:40,390
Now, it's true that we live in poverty, there's no place to live, so how is a garden made?

512
00:32:40,470 --> 00:32:43,170
Not everyone has a garden in their home.

513
00:32:43,250 --> 00:32:44,420
Fair enough.

514
00:32:44,500 --> 00:32:48,280
Learning a recipe or playing a sport or doing something.

515
00:32:48,360 --> 00:32:54,400
There's nothing that we try. Just watching Netflix, watching movies.

516
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:57,270
Often, there are activities in the resume, right?

517
00:32:57,350 --> 00:32:59,352
It says Movies Music Surfing the Web.

518
00:32:59,432 --> 00:33:01,290
What the fuck is Surfing the Web?

519
00:33:01,370 --> 00:33:03,058
Name three websites you go on.

520
00:33:03,138 --> 00:33:04,554
Name three websites.

521
00:33:04,634 --> 00:33:08,541
Reddit doesn't count, Facebook doesn't count, Twitter doesn't count.

522
00:33:08,621 --> 00:33:09,666
Name three websites.

523
00:33:09,746 --> 00:33:11,146
News doesn't count.

524
00:33:11,226 --> 00:33:12,070
There's no one.

525
00:33:12,150 --> 00:33:16,940
When you don't fill any color in your life, you won't even have to color it.

526
00:33:17,020 --> 00:33:21,688
The reason you're stuck is that you're not doing anything special in life.

527
00:33:21,768 --> 00:33:23,333
So add things to your life.

528
00:33:23,413 --> 00:33:24,750
Find some interest.

529
00:33:24,830 --> 00:33:26,041
Keep your phone aside.

530
00:33:26,121 --> 00:33:28,698
I'm saying this because it's always on.

531
00:33:28,778 --> 00:33:30,074
But go out, do something.

532
00:33:30,154 --> 00:33:32,656
So then you'll have something to talk about.

533
00:33:32,736 --> 00:33:34,332
For example, you're in Saudi.

534
00:33:34,412 --> 00:33:35,788
Start playing pickleball.

535
00:33:35,868 --> 00:33:36,168
Okay?

536
00:33:36,248 --> 00:33:37,685
Pickleball is up and coming.

537
00:33:37,765 --> 00:33:39,306
It's very famous in America.

538
00:33:39,386 --> 00:33:41,523
It's also in the Middle East.

539
00:33:41,603 --> 00:33:44,245
So it's a very fun exercise and also a fun game.

540
00:33:44,325 --> 00:33:47,487
When you play that, you'll have something to talk about.

541
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:51,030
If the other person plays, they'll tell you four techniques.

542
00:33:51,290 --> 00:33:53,930
And then you'll have some sort of a conversation.

543
00:33:54,010 --> 00:33:58,650
If you're in a meeting and you have to talk about something, you have an activity over the weekend,

544
00:33:58,730 --> 00:34:04,337
and you say, I went there, I did jet skiing, or I'm taking paragliding classes,

545
00:34:04,417 --> 00:34:06,210
or I'm doing this or that.

546
00:34:06,290 --> 00:34:12,010
Again, I'm not saying that you should take the expensive hobby and invest half of your salary there. I'm not saying that.

547
00:34:12,090 --> 00:34:13,490
But do something.

548
00:34:13,570 --> 00:34:16,250
Add something to your life, learn scuba diving.

549
00:34:16,330 --> 00:34:18,150
If you like climbing mountains.

550
00:34:18,230 --> 00:34:22,350
So do something about it. Do something that you have something to talk about.

551
00:34:22,430 --> 00:34:25,650
My friend Salman, he used to live in Dubai.

552
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:28,650
He had only one goal.

553
00:34:28,730 --> 00:34:31,810
That I don't want to spend my weekends with Indians.

554
00:34:31,890 --> 00:34:33,850
I don't want to make friends.

555
00:34:33,930 --> 00:34:39,970
If I come to this country where there are 200 nationalities, I want to keep my group separate.

556
00:34:40,050 --> 00:34:43,010
And I see him. He has become so fit.

557
00:34:43,090 --> 00:34:45,260
Why does he play volleyball with the British?

558
00:34:45,340 --> 00:34:48,760
He plays squash. He does so many things.

559
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:52,760
So in activities, obviously, he also likes to participate in activities.

560
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:56,760
So your wife decides your tribe and vice versa.

561
00:34:56,840 --> 00:34:59,760
So if your tribe is all going there, then you will also go.

562
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:03,760
Two days you will suck at volleyball, the third day you will learn.

563
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:05,760
So that was his goal.

564
00:35:05,840 --> 00:35:10,760
And I see, Mashallah, his weekends are at least very fulfilling.

565
00:35:10,840 --> 00:35:12,270
Now, how is the work going on?

566
00:35:12,350 --> 00:35:13,470
That's a different thing.

567
00:35:13,550 --> 00:35:18,230
So, try to make friends out of your work. Try to make friends outside your culture.

568
00:35:18,310 --> 00:35:22,430
Meet other people, eat their food, learn from them what's going on and what's not.

569
00:35:22,510 --> 00:35:23,750
You get to learn a lot.

570
00:35:23,830 --> 00:35:26,230
We have everything, that's why everything ends.

571
00:35:26,310 --> 00:35:28,030
There's nothing but weather.

572
00:35:28,110 --> 00:35:32,710
Yesterday it was hot, so the weather was two minutes. What will we talk about then?

573
00:35:32,790 --> 00:35:34,150
Because there are no common grounds.

574
00:35:34,230 --> 00:35:39,540
So the more experiences you have in life, the more experiences you have, you'll have something to talk about.

575
00:35:39,620 --> 00:35:39,988
So yeah,

576
00:35:40,068 --> 00:35:46,560
I'll tell you this and this is what happens that you have to socialize and socializing is what takes you forward.

577
00:35:46,640 --> 00:35:52,020
In the corporate world, let's leave it as your performance, what is it? Of course, that counts to a certain degree.

578
00:35:52,100 --> 00:35:58,069
But how much you vibe with your manager or how much he feels connected to you on a human level,

579
00:35:58,149 --> 00:36:00,120
so those are his different points.

580
00:36:00,200 --> 00:36:01,120
I know this guy.

581
00:36:01,200 --> 00:36:06,530
Well, that's in the sense of waking up. He used to reach at 6 AM every morning with his CEO for golf.

582
00:36:06,610 --> 00:36:10,530
That's another thing. I'm not saying you should be a servant.

583
00:36:10,610 --> 00:36:13,530
What I'm trying to say is, try to add more flavor in your life.

584
00:36:13,610 --> 00:36:16,530
Try to make your weekends more fun.

585
00:36:16,610 --> 00:36:20,530
Other than the fact that you go and eat chicken karahi or go to Delhi Darbar and eat nihari.

586
00:36:20,610 --> 00:36:24,530
Or you watch cricket or spend time at home. Don't do that.

587
00:36:24,610 --> 00:36:27,530
Don't do this to yourself. Add more and more activities.

588
00:36:27,610 --> 00:36:29,530
You're in Saudi. I know weather is a bitch.

589
00:36:29,610 --> 00:36:33,610
But you can find many ways around that. There's so much to do.

590
00:36:33,940 --> 00:36:37,540
I really wish there was Top Golf here. I really like it.

591
00:36:37,620 --> 00:36:42,380
For the longest time, I went to Doha that day. I had a stopover.

592
00:36:42,460 --> 00:36:48,420
So I went to Doha and when my friend gave me the option of playing snooker, I said, yes, please do it.

593
00:36:48,500 --> 00:36:50,580
I haven't played snooker in a while.

594
00:36:50,660 --> 00:36:54,540
And I played pretty well for someone who hadn't played for a year or two.

595
00:36:54,620 --> 00:36:58,620
So since that day, I really want to play.

596
00:36:58,700 --> 00:37:01,390
Now, there are snooker clubs here.

597
00:37:01,470 --> 00:37:05,390
I used to play in snooker clubs but none of my friends know how to play snooker.

598
00:37:05,470 --> 00:37:07,390
I don't have that many friends now.

599
00:37:07,470 --> 00:37:09,390
Now it's even less.

600
00:37:09,470 --> 00:37:13,390
So, I'm just, now I feel very desperate.

601
00:37:13,470 --> 00:37:17,390
Put it on Instagram, if anyone knows how to play snooker, play with me.

602
00:37:17,470 --> 00:37:19,390
It feels weird.

603
00:37:19,470 --> 00:37:22,390
But yeah, I've been meaning to do that for so long.

604
00:37:22,470 --> 00:37:24,390
I really wish there was Top Golf here.

605
00:37:24,470 --> 00:37:26,390
I would have made a basket of balls.

606
00:37:26,470 --> 00:37:29,250
I would have taken 100 balls and would have shot and scored.

607
00:37:29,520 --> 00:37:30,291
I enjoy it.

608
00:37:30,371 --> 00:37:32,846
But here there is no such thing.

609
00:37:32,926 --> 00:37:36,420
So things are much much boring here.

610
00:37:36,500 --> 00:37:40,565
But here I have seen people go out for a dive.

611
00:37:40,645 --> 00:37:44,380
My own brother-in-law, he is very outdoorsy.

612
00:37:44,460 --> 00:37:48,272
He has a special car for off-roading.

613
00:37:48,352 --> 00:37:51,680
He has bought a hut for weekends.

614
00:37:51,760 --> 00:37:56,510
And he is very fond of water sports. So like he is always diving.

615
00:37:56,590 --> 00:37:57,290
here and there.

616
00:37:57,370 --> 00:37:59,658
So, Mashallah, it is a very fulfilling life.

617
00:37:59,738 --> 00:38:02,522
Again, the more you fill your life with experiences,

618
00:38:02,602 --> 00:38:07,310
you will never know that the person sitting in front of you will also get the same shock.

619
00:38:07,390 --> 00:38:11,707
But you will know when you have something to talk about or something to do.

620
00:38:11,787 --> 00:38:16,778
So you will find a lot of common grounds where you will be able to connect with a lot of people.

621
00:38:16,858 --> 00:38:19,416
But it will only come out when you have something.

622
00:38:19,496 --> 00:38:23,370
Try to add more and more activities, whether they are sports or anything.

623
00:38:23,450 --> 00:38:29,370
Whether it's sporting, or a hobby, or going to a museum, or whatever, do something.

624
00:38:29,450 --> 00:38:36,370
Make sure every Saturday, okay, you wake up a little early. It's not necessary to wake up at 7 AM, or 9 AM, or 10 AM.

625
00:38:36,450 --> 00:38:39,962
But make sure you're going somewhere.

626
00:38:40,042 --> 00:38:43,287
Go to a small museum, or go to a park.

627
00:38:43,367 --> 00:38:44,370
Do something.

628
00:38:44,450 --> 00:38:50,450
Whenever I'm very fond of museums, it's a different story. I can't retain them in my memory.

629
00:38:50,630 --> 00:38:54,550
But at least for that moment I enjoy and I feel very fulfilled.

630
00:38:54,630 --> 00:39:03,550
So whenever I have been to the Natural History Museum or the Ricks Museum in Amsterdam or the Holocaust Museum.

631
00:39:03,630 --> 00:39:10,550
It wasn't a Holocaust Museum, it was a Jewish history museum and the vibe there was very off.

632
00:39:10,630 --> 00:39:12,645
And then the Jewish guy, he was like,

633
00:39:12,725 --> 00:39:16,588
he thought that this Pakistani guy came because he was following me.

634
00:39:16,668 --> 00:39:18,090
I will tell you the story later.

635
00:39:18,170 --> 00:39:22,090
Or else concentration camps will be set up, etc.

636
00:39:22,170 --> 00:39:26,090
Wherever I have gone, I have barely ever found another Pakistani.

637
00:39:26,170 --> 00:39:28,090
Because they have no interest.

638
00:39:28,170 --> 00:39:31,090
I have found a lot of Indian families, a lot of South Indian families.

639
00:39:31,170 --> 00:39:35,090
They take a lot of interest in learning about things.

640
00:39:35,170 --> 00:39:40,090
I think one of the reasons for this is that if the middle class is coming up, they have more money to spend.

641
00:39:40,170 --> 00:39:44,170
So they spend on their… But I think it also comes from within.

642
00:39:44,740 --> 00:39:45,889
It's a matter of interest.

643
00:39:45,969 --> 00:39:47,434
Our people don't have interest.

644
00:39:47,514 --> 00:39:52,260
They want to eat Doner Kebab wherever they want to go and don't want to try local things.

645
00:39:52,340 --> 00:39:55,892
Okay, Halal, Haram aside, you can eat vegetables, right?

646
00:39:55,972 --> 00:39:58,328
I tried Indonesian thing in Amsterdam.

647
00:39:58,408 --> 00:39:59,444
It was really bad.

648
00:39:59,524 --> 00:40:00,826
But at least I tried.

649
00:40:00,906 --> 00:40:01,260
Anyway.

650
00:40:01,340 --> 00:40:03,342
So they don't spend on their experiences.

651
00:40:03,422 --> 00:40:06,221
When they don't do it, so they have nothing to talk about.

652
00:40:06,301 --> 00:40:09,801
That's why they go around and whether it's Chicago or Shikarpur,

653
00:40:09,881 --> 00:40:11,100
they have the same topics.

654
00:40:11,630 --> 00:40:17,722
They only change their global positioning, their lifestyle, eating, drinking, socializing,

655
00:40:17,802 --> 00:40:21,350
media exposure, they keep what they left Pakistan.

656
00:40:21,430 --> 00:40:26,350
Which is why they can't mentally grow. They get money, but they can't mentally grow.

657
00:40:26,430 --> 00:40:34,350
So my advice for you and all of you is to fill your life with colors and those colors can only be achieved through experiences.

658
00:40:34,430 --> 00:40:39,430
You can know about a certain city, you can know about a certain place.

659
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:40,712
Go somewhere, explore.

660
00:40:40,792 --> 00:40:42,064
Duniya bahut badi hai.

661
00:40:42,144 --> 00:40:43,510
There's so much to learn.

662
00:40:43,590 --> 00:40:46,941
And there's so much fun in learning random things.

663
00:40:47,021 --> 00:40:49,240
At least I find a lot of fun in that.

664
00:40:49,320 --> 00:40:56,240
So do that. Apne aapko curious rakhein, sawalat karein aur apne aapko khol ke rakhein. Then you'll have so much to talk about.

665
00:40:56,320 --> 00:40:59,891
Now I'm not saying ke phir aapne annoy karne lag jaye hai har kisi ko.

666
00:40:59,971 --> 00:41:03,444
Woh vegan wali baat nahi karni ki har jagah jaake shor karna hai.

667
00:41:03,524 --> 00:41:04,570
Haan main to vegan ho.

668
00:41:04,650 --> 00:41:05,840
Ek kisi ke ghar gaya tha.

669
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:07,540
He said, we are atheists.

670
00:41:07,620 --> 00:41:09,040
So I said, what is this question?

671
00:41:09,120 --> 00:41:13,180
I mean, the person asks how is the weather, how is the weather, how was the journey?

672
00:41:13,260 --> 00:41:14,380
We are atheists.

673
00:41:14,460 --> 00:41:15,380
What the fuck man?

674
00:41:15,460 --> 00:41:19,580
So anyway, so yeah, add more colors to your life.

675
00:41:19,660 --> 00:41:20,920
You'll have a lot to talk about.

676
